// time — constructs the engine does not support yet are accepted (they fall
// back to the legacy matcher at runtime), while truly invalid syntax still
// fails (a Ruby SyntaxError / RegexpError).
let rx_lenient = map_new ();
// Named groups seen so far in the pattern being parsed: the number (for
// `\k<name>`) and the body (for `\g<name>`, which re-matches the group's
// pattern at the call site). Cleared at the start of every parse.
let rx_gnums = map_new ();
// ...and EVERY number a name was given, comma-joined: `(?<a>x)(?<b>y)(?<a>z)`
// is legal, and ruby answers the LAST group of that name that participated
// (#[], #named_captures) while listing the name once, where it first appears.
